            "args_json": "{\"path\": \"./DIFF_PANEL_ANALYSIS.md\", \"content\": \"# Diff Panel Rework Analysis: Rust → Lua+Plugin\\n\\n## Current Architecture\\n\\n### Data Structures (crates/kn9t-tui/src/diff_viewer.rs)\\n- `DiffLine` (enum): Context, Added, Removed\\n- `DiffHunk`: old_start, old_count, new_start, new_count, lines vec\\n- `DiffFile`: path, hunks vec\\n- `DiffViewer` (widget state):\\n  - `files: Vec<DiffFile>` — parsed diff data\\n  - `current_file/current_hunk/cursor_line` — nav state\\n  - `scroll: usize` — vertical scroll position\\n  - `split_mode: bool` — side-by-side vs unified\\n  - `fullscreen: bool` — fullscreen vs embedded\\n  - `comments: Vec<LineComment>` — user comments\\n  - `selected_line/commenting/comment_input` — comment UI state\\n  - `show_file_tree/file_tree_selected` — sidebar state\\n  - `line_hits/last_area` — mouse hit areas\\n  - `LineComment` — file, line, comment text\\n\\n### Key Methods (DiffViewer impl)\\n**Navigation:**\\n- `next_file()`, `prev_file()`, `select_file(idx)`\\n- `next_hunk()`, `prev_hunk()`\\n- `cursor_up()`, `cursor_down()`\\n- `scroll_up(delta)`, `scroll_down(delta)`\\n- `toggle_split_mode()`, `toggle_fullscreen()`, `toggle_file_tree()`\\n\\n**Interaction:**\\n- `handle_click(x, y)` — mouse selection\\n- `handle_click_at(x, y)` — file tree + diff click routing\\n- `handle_scroll(delta)` — mouse wheel\\n\\n**Comments:**\\n- `start_comment()` — enable comment input on line\\n- `add_comment()` — save comment\\n- `cancel_comment()` — discard comment\\n- `has_comment_at()`, `get_comment_at()`\\n- `format_comments()` — return all comments as text\\n\\n**Rendering:**\\n- `render(&mut self, area, buf, theme)` — main render (mutable for line_hits)\\n- `render_file_tree(area, buf)` — sidebar\\n- `render_split_mut(area, buf, theme)` — side-by-side view\\n- `render_unified_mut(area, buf, theme)` — unified view\\n- `render_footer(area, buf)`\\n- `render_comment_overlay(area, buf)`\\n\\n**Helpers:**\\n- `file_status(idx)` → Modified/Added/Deleted\\n- `file_stats(idx)` → (additions, deletions)\\n- `current_file()`, `current_hunk_data()`\\n\\n### Integration Points\\n\\n#### app.rs (App struct)\\n```rust\\npub diff_viewer: Option<crate::diff_viewer::DiffViewer>,\\n```\\n\\n**Lifecycle:**\\n- `open_git_diff()` — runs `git diff`, parses, creates DiffViewer\\n- `close_diff_viewer()` — takes comments, appends to input, drops viewer\\n\\n**Input Handling:**\\n- Diff keys intercepted in `handle_key()` before overlay/screen routing\\n- `handle_overlay_key()` handles diff-specific keys (Esc, j/k, [/], u/f/c/n/p/b)\\n- Lua keymap dispatch first, then built-in defaults\\n\\n**Actions (keybind.rs):**\\n- `OpenDiff` — creates viewer via `open_git_diff()`\\n- `DiffNextHunk`, `DiffPrevHunk`, `DiffNextFile`, `DiffPrevFile`\\n- `DiffCursorUp`, `DiffCursorDown`, `DiffToggleSplit`, `DiffToggleFullscreen`, `DiffToggleTree`\\n- `DiffComment`, `DiffClose`\\n\\n#### render.rs (ui/render.rs)\\n**Two render paths:**\\n\\n1. **Fullscreen mode** (render_chat_overlays, line 134-138):\\n   ```rust\\n   if viewer.fullscreen {\\n       viewer.render(area, buf, theme)\\n   }\\n   ```\\n\\n2. **Embedded mode** (render_native_view, line 318-321):\\n   ```rust\\n   \\\"diff\\\" => {\\n       if let Some(viewer) = app.diff_viewer {\\n           viewer.render(area, buf, theme)\\n       }\\n   }\\n   ```\\n   — Placed by Lua in `render_ui()` layout\\n\\n### Key Features to Preserve\\n\\n1. **Data Parsing**\\n   - Git unified diff format parsing → DiffFile/DiffHunk/DiffLine\\n   - File status detection (Added/Modified/Deleted)\\n   - Line stats (+N -M)\\n\\n2. **Navigation**\\n   - File list (next/prev/select)\\n   - Hunk navigation (next/prev hunk header)\\n   - Line cursor (up/down with auto-scroll)\\n   - Scroll mode (Page Up/Down + wheel)\\n   - File tree sidebar (toggle, click to select)\\n\\n3. **Rendering**\\n   - Split mode (side-by-side) vs unified\\n   - Syntax highlighting (per language)\\n   - Colors (status: green/yellow/red, +/- lines)\\n   - File tree sidebar with status indicators\\n   - Fullscreen overlay + embedded layout\\n\\n4. **Comments**\\n   - Add comment on line (Ctrl+Enter or click)\\n   - Comment overlay (text input)\\n   - Format comments for final input\\n   - Persist on close, append to input\\n\\n5. **Mouse Support**\\n   - Click to select line / open comment\\n   - Click file tree to select file\\n   - Scroll wheel delta\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Proposed Rework: Plugin + Lua\\n\\n### Phase 1: Plugin Side (Rust)\\n\\n**New plugin: `kn9t-plugin-diff`**\\n\\nResponsibilities:\\n- Diff parsing (git diff → structured data)\\n- Syntax highlighting helpers (defer to existing code)\\n- Mouse hit-test geometry (cursor in box)\\n\\n**Exported via plugin SDK:**\\n```rust\\npub struct DiffPanel {\\n    pub files: Vec<DiffFile>,\\n    pub current_file: usize,\\n    pub current_hunk: usize,\\n    pub scroll: usize,\\n    pub split_mode: bool,\\n    pub fullscreen: bool,\\n    pub comments: Vec<LineComment>,\\n    pub selected_line: Option<(usize, usize, usize, u32)>,\\n    pub commenting: bool,\\n    pub comment_input: String,\\n    pub cursor_line: usize,\\n    pub show_file_tree: bool,\\n    pub file_tree_selected: usize,\\n}\\n\\nimpl DiffPanel {\\n    // Setters only — Lua drives nav/rendering\\n    pub fn set_current_file(&mut self, idx: usize) { ... }\\n    pub fn set_cursor_line(&mut self, idx: usize) { ... }\\n    pub fn set_scroll(&mut self, offset: usize) { ... }\\n    pub fn set_split_mode(&mut self, enabled: bool) { ... }\\n    pub fn set_fullscreen(&mut self, enabled: bool) { ... }\\n    pub fn toggle_file_tree(&mut self) { ... }\\n    pub fn set_commenting(&mut self, enabled: bool, line: Option<u32>) { ... }\\n    pub fn add_comment(&mut self, file_path: &str, line: u32, text: &str) { ... }\\n    pub fn cancel_comment(&mut self) { ... }\\n    \\n    // Query only — Lua reads for rendering\\n    pub fn get_files(&self) -> &[DiffFile] { ... }\\n    pub fn get_current_file(&self) -> Option<&DiffFile> { ... }\\n    pub fn get_file_status(&self, idx: usize) -> FileStatus { ... }\\n    pub fn get_file_stats(&self, idx: usize) -> (usize, usize) { ... }\\n    pub fn get_comments_for_file(&self, path: &str) -> Vec<(u32, &str)> { ... }\\n    pub fn format_all_comments(&self) -> String { ... }\\n}\\n\\n// Commands exposed to Lua\\npub fn parse_git_diff(diff_text: &str) -> DiffPanel { ... }\\n```\\n\\n**Plugin responsibilities:**\\n- NOT rendering — only data + state management\\n- NOT keybinding — Lua handles all input\\n- NOT mouse handling — Lua handles click dispatch\\n\\n### Phase 2: Lua Side (Rendering + Control)\\n\\n**Location:** `~/.kn9t/plugins/diff.lua` (user-customizable)\\n\\n**Responsibilities:**\\n1. **State management** (in Lua table):\\n   ```lua\\n   local diff = {\\n       panel = nil,  -- DiffPanel reference\\n       view_mode = \\\"split\\\",  -- \\\"split\\\" or \\\"unified\\\"\\n       scroll = 0,\\n       cursor_line = 0,\\n       -- ... other UI state\\n   }\\n   ```\\n\\n2. **Rendering** (in `render_ui()`):\\n   ```lua\\n   function render_ui()\\n       -- Lua builds the entire diff display\\n       -- Calls panel methods to get data\\n       -- Renders with custom colors/fonts/layout\\n       return {\\n           type = \\\"vbox\\\",\\n           children = {\\n               -- File tree sidebar\\n               { type = \\\"hbox\\\", width = 30, child = render_file_tree() },\\n               -- Diff content\\n               { type = \\\"vbox\\\", child = render_diff_content() },\\n               -- Footer\\n               { type = \\\"hbox\\\", height = 2, child = render_footer() },\\n           }\\n       }\\n   end\\n   ```\\n\\n3. **Input handling** (in Lua keymap):\\n   ```lua\\n   kn9t.map(\\\"diff:next_file\\\", function() \\n       diff.panel:set_current_file(diff.panel:get_current_file_idx() + 1)\\n   end)\\n   kn9t.map(\\\"diff:prev_hunk\\\", function()\\n       -- Navigate to prev hunk in virtual line list\\n   end)\\n   -- ... all keybinds now in Lua\\n   ```\\n\\n4. **Mouse handling** (in render_ui() click areas):\\n   ```lua\\n   -- Register clickable regions during render\\n   -- file_tree[i].on_click -> set_current_file(i)\\n   -- diff_line[j].on_click -> set_cursor_line(j) / start_comment()\\n   ```\\n\\n5. **Comments overlay**:\\n   ```lua\\n   function render_comment_overlay()\\n       if diff.panel.commenting then\\n           return render_input_box(diff.panel.comment_input)\\n       end\\n   end\\n   ```\\n\\n### Phase 3: Integration (Rust)\\n\\n**Changes to app.rs:**\\n\\n1. Replace `pub diff_viewer: Option<DiffViewer>` with:\\n   ```rust\\n   pub diff_panel: Option<Arc<Mutex<DiffPanel>>>,  // via plugin\\n   ```\\n\\n2. Remove all diff-specific action handling from `execute_action()`:\\n   ```rust\\n   // DELETE these:\\n   // Action::DiffNextHunk | ... => { viewer methods }\\n   // \\n   // Keep only Action::OpenDiff, which calls plugin\\n   // and creates the initial state\\n   ```\\n\\n3. `open_git_diff()` now:\\n   ```rust\\n   fn open_git_diff(&mut self) {\\n       let diff_text = run_git_diff();\\n       let panel = plugin::diff::parse_git_diff(&diff_text);\\n       self.diff_panel = Some(Arc::new(Mutex::new(panel)));\\n       // Lua takes over from here\\n   }\\n   ```\\n\\n4. `close_diff_viewer()` now:\\n   ```rust\\n   fn close_diff_viewer(&mut self) {\\n       let Some(panel) = self.diff_panel.take() else { return };\\n       let comments = panel.lock().unwrap().format_all_comments();\\n       // ... append to input\\n   }\\n   ```\\n\\n**Changes to render.rs:**\\n\\n1. Replace fullscreen diff render with Lua-based display\\n   (Lua `render_ui()` handles it)\\n\\n2. Keep `render_native_view(\\\"diff\\\", ...)` only as a fallback\\n   or remove it entirely (Lua owns layout)\\n\\n3. Remove all DiffViewer rendering code:\\n   - `render_split_mut()`, `render_unified_mut()`\\n   - `render_file_tree()`, `render_footer()`\\n   - `render_comment_overlay()`\\n\\n**Changes to keybind.rs:**\\n\\n1. Keep Action enum (Actions are still the transport)\\n2. Remove built-in key→action mappings for diff actions\\n3. Let default_tui.lua (or user config) define all bindings\\n\\n**Changes to handle_overlay_key():**\\n\\n1. Remove all diff-specific logic\\n2. Let Lua keymap handle everything via `dispatch_keymap()`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Features Preserved ✓\\n\\n| Feature | Current | New |\\n|---------|---------|-----|\\n| Parse git diff | Rust parser | Plugin (Rust) |\\n| Parse hunks/lines | Rust | Plugin (Rust) |\\n| File status detection | Rust | Plugin (Rust) |\\n| Split/unified toggle | Rust action | Lua action |\\n| Navigation (hunk/file) | Rust nav methods | Lua nav logic |\\n| Syntax highlighting | Rust highlight_diff_line() | Lua calls plugin helpers |\\n| File tree sidebar | Rust render | Lua render |\\n| Comments (add/delete) | Rust UI | Lua input + plugin state |\\n| Mouse support | Rust hit-test | Lua click areas |\\n| Fullscreen overlay | Rust render overlay | Lua render |\\n| Embedded in layout | Lua native view | Lua render directly |\\n| Scroll wheel | Rust handler | Lua handler + plugin |\\n| Line selection | Rust cursor | Lua cursor + plugin |\\n| Color theming | Rust | Lua (full control) |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Benefits\\n\\n1. **Lua controls UX** — Users can fully customize layout, colors, keybinds, behavior\\n2. **Smaller Rust surface** — Only data structures + parsing\\n3. **Easier to maintain** — Changes to UI don't touch Rust code\\n4. **Plugin ecosystem** — Other plugins can render diffs too (git, pr review, etc.)\\n5. **No Actions bloat** — Actions list shrinks; Lua actions replace them\\n6. **Composable** — Lua can embed diff in any layout (sidebar, modal, pane, etc.)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Migration Path\\n\\n1. **Keep DiffViewer** for backward compat\\n2. **Create plugin** with new DiffPanel API\\n3. **Add Lua render_ui entry point** for diff\\n4. **Migrate default_tui.lua** to use new plugin\\n5. **Deprecate** old DiffViewer in favor of plugin\\n6. **Remove** in next major version\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Example Lua Config (Post-Migration)\\n\\n```lua\\n-- ~/.kn9t/plugins/diff.lua\\nlocal kn9t = require('kn9t')\\n\\n-- Create diff panel state\\nlocal diff_state = {\\n    panel = nil,\\n    view_mode = 'split',\\n}\\n\\n-- Register commands\\nkn9t.register_command({\\n    name = 'diff_open',\\n    description = 'Open git diff',\\n    handler = function()\\n        local diff_text = kn9t.exec_bash('git diff HEAD')\\n        diff_state.panel = kn9t.plugin.diff.parse(diff_text)\\n    end\\n})\\n\\n-- Keybindings\\nkn9t.map('diff:toggle_split', function()\\n    diff_state.view_mode = diff_state.view_mode == 'split' and 'unified' or 'split'\\nend)\\n\\nkn9t.map('diff:next_file', function()\\n    if diff_state.panel then\\n        local idx = diff_state.panel:get_current_file() + 1\\n        diff_state.panel:set_current_file(idx)\\n    end\\nend)\\n\\n-- Rendering\\nkn9t.register_ui_handler(function(width, height)\\n    if not diff_state.panel then return nil end\\n    \\n    return {\\n        type = 'vbox',\\n        width = width,\\n        height = height,\\n        children = {\\n            -- Render the full diff UI here\\n            render_diff_panel(diff_state.panel, width, height)\\n        }\\n    }\\nend)\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Open Questions\\n\\n1. **Parsing location**: Should unified diff parsing stay in kn9t-core or move to plugin?\\n   → Plugin (easier versioning, optional)\\n\\n2. **Syntax highlighting**: Keep in core or move to plugin?\\n   → Keep in core (shared with tool diffs), plugin calls it\\n\\n3. **Keybind defaults**: Where do we define default diff keybinds?\\n   → In default_tui.lua (same as other UI)\\n\\n4. **State persistence**: Should diff state survive Lua reload?\\n   → No, close diff on config reload (cleaner)\\n\\n5. **Multiple diffs**: Can Lua render two diffs side-by-side?\\n   → Yes! Create multiple DiffPanel instances in Lua state\\n\\n\"}",
