              │ DiffNextHunk => v.next_hunk()    │\\n│                          │ DiffCursorDown => v.cursor_down()│\\n│                          │ DiffToggleSplit => toggle()      │\\n│                          │ DiffComment => start_comment()   │\\n│                          └──────────────────────────────────┘\\n│                                  │\\n│                                  ▼\\n│  DiffViewer (diff_viewer.rs)\\n│  ├─ State: files, current_file, cursor_line, scroll, comments\\n│  ├─ Navigation: next_file(), prev_file(), next_hunk(), prev_hunk()\\n│  ├─ Interaction: handle_click(), handle_scroll(), start_comment()\\n│  ├─ Rendering: render(), render_split_mut(), render_unified_mut()\\n│  │             render_file_tree(), render_comment_overlay()\\n│  └─ Comments: add_comment(), get_comment_at()\\n│\\n│  render_chat() in render.rs ◄────────────┬─────────────────┐\\n│                                          │                 │\\n│                    ┌─────────────────────┘                 │\\n│                    │ Check diff_viewer.is_some()           │\\n│                    │ AND fullscreen                        │\\n│                    ▼                                       │\\n│         ┌──────────────────────────┐              ┌──────────┐\\n│         │ render_chat_overlays()   │              │ Lua      │\\n│         │ ├─ viewer.render()       │              │ render   │\\n│         │ └─ [fullscreen overlay]  │              │_ui()     │\\n│         └──────────────────────────┘              └──────────┘\\n│\\n│         render_native_view(\\\"diff\\\") ◄──────────────┐\\n│         (called by Lua if placed in layout)       │\\n│         └─ calls viewer.render()                  │\\n│\\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\\n```\\n\\n**Problems:**\\n- Keybinds hardcoded in Rust (handle_overlay_key)\\n- Rendering tightly coupled to DiffViewer struct\\n- No way to customize UI without recompiling\\n- 500+ lines of diff 