nend\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Migration Path\\n\\n### Phase 1: Parallel Implementation (Week 1-2)\\n1. Create `kn9t-plugin-diff` crate\\n2. Extract `DiffPanel` from `DiffViewer`\\n3. Implement `parse_git_diff()` in plugin\\n4. Write unit tests for parser and API\\n\\n### Phase 2: New UI Layer (Week 2-3)\\n1. Write `default_tui.lua` with diff support\\n2. Render diff via Lua (not Rust)\\n3. Test all navigation, comments, mouse\\n4. Keep old DiffViewer working in parallel\\n\\n### Phase 3: Migration (Week 3-4)\\n1. Mark `DiffViewer` as deprecated\\n2. Switch default to use plugin\\n3. Update docs\\n4. Gather user feedback\\n\\n### Phase 4: Cleanup (Week 5+)\\n1. Remove old `DiffViewer` code (next major version)\\n2. Remove hardcoded diff actions from `keybind.rs`\\n\\n### Compatibility\\n- Old configs still work (Action::OpenDiff still exists)\\n- Lua keybinds override Rust defaults\\n- Gradual deprecation (no breaking changes immediately)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Benefits\\n\\n### For Users\\n- ✓ **Full UI customization** — Layout, colors, fonts all in Lua\\n- ✓ **Extensible actions** — Add custom commands beyond navigation\\n- ✓ **Better integration** — Diff can embed in any Lua layout\\n- ✓ **Easier workflows** — Could add \\\"save review\\\", \\\"share diff\\\", etc.\\n\\n### For Maintainers\\n- ✓ **Smaller core** — 1650 lines → 50 lines of diff code\\n- ✓ **Easier bugs** — Diff issues don't require Rust rebuild\\n- ✓ **Composable** — Plugin pattern can be applied elsewhere\\n- ✓ **Proven architecture** — Same as \\\"native view\\\" pattern (transcript, status)\\n\\n### For the Ecosystem\\n- ✓ **Plugin precedent** — Other tools can follow (PR viewer, etc.)\\n- ✓ **Less C++/Rust** — More Lua; easier contributions\\n- ✓ **Modular** — Diff functionality can be reused in other tools\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Code Metrics\\n\\n| Metric | Before | After | Change |\\n|--------|--------|-------|--------|\\n| Rust diff code | 1650 lines | ~50 lines | **-97%** |\\n| diff_viewer.rs | 1000 lines | 0 | **deleted** |\\n| keybind.rs (diff) | 50 lines | 0 | **deleted** |\\n| render.rs (diff) | 400 lines | 0 | **deleted** |\\n| app.rs (diff) | 200 lines | ~50 lines | **-75%** |\\n| Action enum (diff) | 11 variants | 1 variant | **-91%** |\\n| Lua config (new) | N/A | ~500 lines | **+500** |\\n| Plugin (new) | N/A | ~300 lines | **+300** |\\n| **Total code** | 1650 Rust | 350 Rust + 500 Lua | **Same!** |\\n\\n**Key insight:** Not removing code, *moving* it to user-editable layer + plugin.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Open Questions\\n\\n1. **Should diff parsing move to core?**\\n   - Current: In plugin ✓\\n   - Alternative: In kn9t-core (shared by other tools)\\n   - Recommendation: Stay in plugin (easier versioning, optional)\\n\\n2. **Should syntax highlighting stay in core?**\\n   - Current: Yes ✓ (plugin calls it)\\n   - Recommendation: Yes (used by tool diffs too)\\n\\n3. **What's the default keybind mapping?**\\n   - Answer: In `default_tui.lua`\\n   - Users can override in `~/.kn9t/plugins/diff.lua`\\n\\n4. **Can Lua render two diffs side-by-side?**\\n   - Answer: Yes! Create multiple DiffPanel instances\\n   - Current Rust can't do this ✗\\n\\n5. **How do we handle diff close?**\\n   - Answer: Same as now — capture comments, append to input\\n   - Lua can bind any key to Action::DiffClose (or new action)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Risks & Mitigations\\n\\n| Risk | Severity | Mitigation |\\n|------|----------|-----------|\\n| Users hate losing Rust impl | Low | Keep old impl for 1 version, migrate gradually |\\n| Lua diff is slower | Low | Profile before committing; likely same speed |\\n| Lua API too limited | Medium | Design API first, user-test before coding |\\n| Diff parsing bugs in plugin | Low | Thorough unit tests; same parser, just moved |\\n| Comments don't work right | Low | Same logic, just moved to plugin + Lua |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n\\n1. **Review this design** with team\\n2. **Approve API surface** for DiffPanel (setters/getters)\\n3. **Start Phase 1:*