l\\n  ├─ High-level architecture\\n  └─ Do we want to proceed?\\n     ├─ YES → Continue\\n     └─ NO → Discuss concerns, revisit\\n\\nRead: DIFF_REWORK_SUMMARY.md (10 min)\\n  ├─ Understand phases\\n  ├─ Review migration path\\n  ├─ Check risks & mitigations\\n  └─ Approve direction?\\n     ├─ YES → Assign work\\n     └─ NO → Which part needs redesign?\\n\\nRead: DIFF_PANEL_ANALYSIS.md (15 min)\\n  ├─ Review API design\\n  ├─ Check feature preservation\\n  ├─ Finalize 5 open questions\\n  └─ Approved for coding?\\n     ├─ YES → Start Phase 1\\n     └─ NO → Iterate on API\\n\\nRead: DIFF_REWORK_ARCHITECTURE.md (20 min)\\n  ├─ Review all diagrams\\n  ├─ Trace data flows\\n  ├─ Understand before/after\\n  └─ Ready to implement?\\n     ├─ YES → Create plugin scaffold\\n     └─ NO → Review earlier docs again\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## How to Use These Documents\\n\\n### If you have **5 minutes:**\\nRead **DIFF_REWORK_QUICK_REF.md** only.\\n\\n### If you have **15 minutes:**\\nRead **DIFF_REWORK_QUICK_REF.md** + **DIFF_REWORK_SUMMARY.md** (first half).\\n\\n### If you have **30 minutes:**\\nRead **DIFF_REWORK_SUMMARY.md** + **DIFF_PANEL_ANALYSIS.md** (API section).\\n\\n### If you're **implementing this:**\\nRead all four documents in this order:\\n1. DIFF_REWORK_QUICK_REF.md (overview)\\n2. DIFF_REWORK_SUMMARY.md (phases + migration)\\n3. DIFF_PANEL_ANALYSIS.md (API detail)\\n4. DIFF_REWORK_ARCHITECTURE.md (data flows + diagrams)\\n\\n### If you're **reviewing this proposal:**\\nStart with **DIFF_REWORK_SUMMARY.md**, then review whichever technical sections match your expertise.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Sections by Topic\\n\\n### Understanding the Problem\\n- DIFF_REWORK_SUMMARY.md → \\\"Current State\\\"\\n- DIFF_REWORK_ARCHITECTURE.md → \\\"Current (Monolithic Rust)\\\"\\n- DIFF_PANEL_ANALYSIS.md → \\\"Current Architecture\\\"\\n\\n### Understanding the Solution\\n- DIFF_REWORK_QUICK_REF.md → \\\"How?\\\" (all 3 phases)\\n- DIFF_REWORK_SUMMARY.md → \\\"Proposed Solution\\\"\\n- DIFF_REWORK_ARCHITECTURE.md → \\\"Proposed (Plugin + Lua)\\\"\\n\\n### API Design\\n- DIFF_PANEL_ANALYSIS.md → \\\"Phase 1: Plugin Side (Rust)\\\"\\n- DIFF_PANEL_ANALYSIS.md → \\\"Phase 2: Lua Side\\\"\\n- DIFF_REWORK_ARCHITECTURE.md → \\\"Data Flow\\\"\\n\\n### User Impact\\n- DIFF_REWORK_SUMMARY.md → \\\"User Impact\\\"\\n- DIFF_REWORK_QUICK_REF.md → \\\"User Benefits\\\"\\n- DIFF_PANEL_ANALYSIS.md → \\\"Features Preserved\\\"\\n\\n### Implementation Details\\n- DIFF_PANEL_ANALYSIS.md → \\\"Phase 3: Integration\\\"\\n- DIFF_REWORK_ARCHITECTURE.md → \\\"Data Flow\\\"\\n- DIFF_REWORK_ARCHITECTURE.md → \\\"File Locations: Before → After\\\"\\n\\n### Migration & Compatibility\\n- DIFF_REWORK_SUMMARY.md → \\\"Migration Path\\\"\\n- DIFF_PANEL_ANALYSIS.md → \\\"Open Questions\\\"\\n- DIFF_REWORK_ARCHITECTURE.md → \\\"Testing Strategy\\\"\\n\\n### Code Metrics\\n- DIFF_REWORK_SUMMARY.md → \\\"Code Metrics\\\"\\n- DIFF_REWORK_QUICK_REF.md → \\\"Code Reduction\\\"\\n- DIFF_REWORK_ARCHITECTURE.md → \\\"Code Reduction Summary\\\"\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Key Design Decisions\\n\\n### 1. Where does diff parsing live?\\n**Decision:** In plugin ✓  \\n**Rationale:** Easier versioning, optional, can be used by other tools  \\n**Alternative:** In kn9t-core (rejected: adds core dependency)\\n\\n**See:** DIFF_PANEL_ANALYSIS.md → \\\"Open Questions\\\" #1\\n\\n### 2. Where does syntax highlighting stay?\\n**Decision:** In core ✓  \\n**Rationale:** Used by tool diffs too, complex feature  \\n**Alternative:** Move to plugin (rejected: code duplication)\\n\\n**See:** DIFF_PANEL_ANALYSIS.md → \\\"Open Questions\\\" #2\\n\\n### 3. Where are default keybinds?\\n**Decision:** In default_tui.lua ✓  \\n**Rationale:** Part of UI layout, users can override  \\n**Alternative:** In plugin (rejected: mixes concerns)\\n\\n**See:** DIFF_PANEL_ANALYSIS.md → \\\"Open Questions\\\" #3\\n\\n### 4. Can Lua render multiple diffs side-by-side?\\n**Decision:** Yes ✓  \\n**Rationale:** Plugin API allows multiple DiffP