            "text": "I need to stop and correct the record rather than start writing code. My design documents from the previous turn contain three architectural errors that I should have caught by reading the code before writing them.\n\n## The design I gave you cannot be built as written\n\n**Error 1 — It violates GI-6.** `crates/kn9t-tui/Cargo.toml:7` says: `# R-TUI-010/GI-6: NO kn9t-* dependencies allowed.` My docs repeatedly propose the TUI calling `kn9t_plugin_diff::parse_git_diff(&text)` and storing `Option<Arc<Mutex<DiffPanel>>>` from that crate. That is a direct violation of a hard invariant, and it's the load-bearing element of every one of the four documents.\n\n**Error 2 — Plugin Lua cannot hold or mutate a `DiffPanel` object.** The real mechanism is one-directional and JSON-only (`crates/kn9t-tui/src/lua/plugin_ui.rs:1-23`): a plugin sends Lua source via `ui_register_lua`, then pushes state with `ui_set_state`, and its `render(state)` returns a widget tree. Plugin Lua runs in a locked-down env (`plugin_ui.rs:107-120`) with only `string`/`table`/`math`/`pcall`-type helpers — deliberately **no `kn9t` table at all**, because \"a plugin must not read session state or call HTTP through the UI layer.\" So `panel:set_current_file(...)`, `panel:get_files()`, and `kn9t.map(...)` from plugin Lua — which appear throughout my docs — have nowhere to bind.\n\n**Error 3 — `kn9t.exec_bash('git diff HEAD')` doesn't exist and can't.** `sandbox.rs` nils out `io`, `package`, `loadfile`, `dofile`, and `os.execute`. My example Lua config calls a shell from Lua twice.\n\nI also asserted specific line counts (\"~1000 lines\", \"97% reduction\", the whole metrics table) that I never measured. Those were fabricated.\n\n## What the codebase actually supports\n\nThe good news is that a Lua-driven diff panel is feasible — just via a different seam than I described. Two viable shapes:\n\n- **A. `tui.lua` owns the diff UI.** Keep parsing + `git diff` in Rust (behind `Action::OpenDiff`), expose diff data through the existing `StateSnapshot`/lazy-data path that `kn9t.get_messages` already uses, delete the ~8 Rust render methods, and let the user's `tui.lua` build the widget tree with real `kn9t.map` keybinds and `kn9t.on_click`. This keeps full feature parity and stays inside GI-6.\n- **B. A real external plugin owns it.** The plugin shells out to `git` itself (it's a native process, so that's allowed), ships its `render(state)` Lua via `ui_register_lua`, and pushes hunks through `ui_set_state`. Maximally decoupled — but plugin Lua gets no keybinds or click API, so navigation/comments would need new host plumbing that doesn't exist yet.\n\nThese differ a lot in scope and in who can customize what, so I don't want to pick for you.\n\nOne thing worth flagging for either path: the comment feature currently computes line numbers as `hunk.new_start + line_idx` (`diff_viewer.rs:443`), which counts removed lines and so mis-numbers comments in any hunk containing deletions. Worth fixing during the move rather than porting faithfully.\n\nHow would you like to proceed — A, B, or should I write a corrected design doc for one of them first? I'd also suggest deleting the four `DIFF_*.md` files, since they'd be actively misleading to anyone who reads them; I won't remove them without your go-ahead.",
