            "text": "I now have the full picture, and there's a genuine blocker I need to put in front of you before writing code rather than discovering it halfway through.\n\n## What I confirmed\n\nYour instinct was right on both counts:\n\n**cwd is already delivered per-session, no tool needed.** `get_steering` fires every turn with `{session_id, cwd}` (`crates/kn9t-plugin/src/host.rs:998-1001`), and kn9t-agents-md consumes exactly that (`main.go:103-106`, subscribed at `main.go:290`). So the `git_status` tool's entire justification — main.rs:4-9's claim that \"the plugin protocol gives no way to reach the host API outside a live tool/hook dispatch\" — is **wrong about hooks**. `dispatch_hook_handler` (`plugin.rs:427`) proves the narrower true part: `PluginHook::call` gets `&Value` and no host client, so it can't push `ui_set_state` today.\n\n**The git plugin is over-designed for the wrong reason.** The tool exists mainly as a bootstrap trigger, plus a per-cwd `HashSet` guard, plus a 10-failure teardown heuristic (`poller.rs:58`) that admits it wastes ~30s of polling per closed session.\n\n## The blocker\n\nPlugin-supplied Lua is **render-only**. `prepare_env` (`plugin_ui.rs:107-120`) deliberately withholds the `kn9t` table, with the comment \"a plugin must not read session state or call HTTP through the UI layer.\" Concretely, plugin Lua has no `kn9t.map` and no `kn9t.on_click`.\n\nA diff *view* works today. An **interactive** diff sidebar — j/k cursor, `[`/`]` hunks, click-to-select file, comment entry — does not, because there is no input path from the TUI back to plugin Lua. Nothing in `PluginLuaOp` (Register/SetState/Clear) travels toward the plugin.\n\nSo \"strong B\" needs one of:\n\n1. **New host plumbing** — grant plugin Lua a scoped `kn9t.map`/`on_click`, plus a plugin-bound reverse channel. Real protocol work in `reducer.rs`/`plugin_ui.rs`, and it partly relaxes an isolation boundary that was drawn deliberately.\n2. **Hybrid** — plugin owns git + parsing + pushes hunks via `ui_set_state`; the **user's `tui.lua`** owns the interactive diff UI (it has full `kn9t.map`/`on_click`). Feature parity, no new protocol, but the panel lives in user config, not the plugin.\n3. **View-only in-plugin** — plugin Lua renders a scrollable diff; drop cursor/comments. Smallest, loses features you said to keep.\n\nIndependently, and needed by all three: give `PluginHook` a host client so `get_steering` can bootstrap the poller, letting `git_status` become `hidden: true` or be deleted.\n\nMy recommendation is **2**, and it's a small delta from what you asked: identical division of labour (plugin = git+parse, Lua = UI), just the panel Lua in `tui.lua` instead of shipped from the plugin. It's the only option reaching full parity without loosening the isolation boundary. If you want the panel to ship *with* the plugin, that's option 1 and I'd sequence it: hook-cwd bootstrap first, then the input channel.\n\nWhich way — 1, 2, or 3? And should the `git_status` tool become hidden or be removed outright?",
