            "text": "Both done. Workspace green (47 suites), clippy clean on my code, `xtask -- check` reports zero drift.\n\n## wire.rs corruption — fixed\n\n`gen_wire.rs` had a hardcoded `PINNED_MODEL_TYPES` string listing four fields, while `schema/http.json` defines seven for `GET /models`. Every `generate` run therefore *deleted* `ctx_window`/`max_out`/`price` and broke `model_selector.rs`. Replaced with `model_types_struct(http)`, which derives fields from the schema — the same pattern `session_list_struct` already used.\n\nTwo judgement calls, documented in the code:\n- **Token counts stay `Option<usize>`**, not the generic `u64`, because `model_selector.rs` and the context gauge compare them against other `usize` values — `u64` would only add casts at every use site.\n- **`price` stays `serde_json::Value`**: nothing in the TUI reads it, so naming a struct would be dead code needing sync. I verified `#[serde(default)]` on `Value` yields `Null`, so an omitting server still deserializes.\n\nGuarded by four new tests, notably `model_info_keeps_every_schema_field` — it walks the schema, so adding a field to `GET /models` and forgetting the generator now fails loudly instead of silently dropping it.\n\n## `check` — my earlier report was wrong\n\nI said \"`check` doesn't exist\". It did — wired as `--check` at `main.rs:43`, and `scripts/check-schema.sh` uses that form correctly. I'd invoked the bare word and drew the wrong conclusion from the error. Apologies; the concern about drift detection not holding was unfounded.\n\nWhat I changed is small: it now accepts **both** `check` and `--check` (bare word matches `generate` and is what you'd guess first), and the error/usage text names both instead of claiming only `generate` exists — that misleading message is what fooled me.\n\nVerified end-to-end: appended a line to API.md, `check` exited 1 naming the file; restored, exited 0.\n\n## One thing to note\n\n`wire.rs` now shows as modified — that's the **intended** fix