            "text": "Both confirmed. Here's what's actually going on — and I owe you a correction on the second point.\n\n## 1. Why `install-plugins` \"didn't install\" it — it did\n\nYour run output says:\n\n```\n- kn9t-git-integration (Rust)\n[install-plugins] kn9t-git-integration already installed (use --force to overwrite)\n```\n\nThe exe **is** at `~/.kn9t/plugins/kn9t-git-integration.exe`, and Rust plugins there are auto-discovered — no `[[plugin]]` config entry needed. So my earlier \"add this to config.toml\" advice was wrong; ignore it.\n\n**But there's a real problem I caused:** `~/.kn9t/plugins/` still contains the *old* `kn9t-git-status.exe` alongside the new one. Both will be discovered and spawned. The stale one still registers a `git_status` tool and its own UI panel, so you'd get two git panels and the tool I supposedly deleted. Delete it:\n\n```powershell\nRemove-Item \"$env:USERPROFILE\\.kn9t\\plugins\\kn9t-git-status.exe\"\n```\n\nI should have flagged that when I renamed the crate — a rename leaves the old installed artifact behind, and `install-plugins` has no way to know it's obsolete.\n\nAlso: \"already installed\" means it did **not** copy your fresh build. Use `--force` after rebuilding, or the running exe is whatever was there before.\n\n## 2. The Rust diff viewer — my mistake, not a bug\n\nI need to correct something I implied. **I never deleted the Rust diff viewer.** Going back over what I actually did: I built the plugin-side diff panel and the host primitives to make it possible, but `diff_viewer.rs` (~1000 lines), `Action::OpenDiff`, the 11 diff actions, the `/diff` slash command, and the `\"diff\"` native view are all still in place and wired exactly as before.\n\nSo `F10` and `/diff` giving you the Rust viewer is the *current expected behaviour* — the two implementations coexist right now. Removing the old one is a separate step I haven't done, and I shouldn't have left you thinking otherwise.\n\n## What to actually test\n\nAfter deleting the stale exe and re-running with `--force`, then triggering a plugin reload:\n\n1. **Panel appears** — a `kn9t-git-integration` box with branch/changes/recent commits.\n2. **No `git_status` tool** — check the tools list (Ctrl+T); its absence confirms the hook-based bootstrap replaced it.\n3. **Focus it** — `Ctrl+G`. Border should turn cyan, title shows \"Esc to release\", and the box should grow from 8 to 24 rows.\n4. **`d`** — switches that panel into diff review mode. This is the new panel, distinct from F10's Rust viewer.\n5. **`j`/`k`, `]`/`[`, `n`/`p`, `u`, `b`** — cursor, hunks, files, split/unified, file tree.\n6. **`c`** → type → **Enter** → **`Ctrl+S`** — comment lands in your prompt as `[path:line] text`. Worth checking the line number is right on a hunk containing deletions — that's the bug I fixed.\n7. **`Esc`** — releases focus; `j`/`k` go back to the host.\n\nIf the panel doesn't appear at all, the likely cause is the poller needing a turn to bootstrap (it rides `get_steering`), so send one message first.\n\nWant me to remove the old Rust diff viewer now, so `F10`/`/diff` open the plugin panel instead?",
