            "text": "Still used by tool cards, so no orphan. Done — here's where things stand.\n\n## Completed\n\n**1. Stale plugin removed.** `kn9t-git-status.exe` was locked because PID 24044 was still running — both old and new git plugins were live simultaneously, which is what would have given you duplicate panels and the `git_status` tool I said was gone. Killed that process only, deleted the exe.\n\n**2. `install-plugins --force`.** It reported 6 failures — Windows locks running exes, so `--force` can't overwrite any live plugin. I verified by hash that the installed `kn9t-git-integration.exe` is **byte-identical** to your current build, so nothing needed copying. Worth knowing: `--force` is effectively a no-op for running plugins.\n\n**3. Native Rust diff viewer deleted.** Net **−2285 lines** in `kn9t-tui`:\n\n- `diff_viewer.rs` — gone (~1900 lines with tests)\n- All 12 `Action::Diff*` variants and their `parse_action` names\n- The diff branch in `handle_overlay_key`, `handle_key`, `handle_welcome_key`, `handle_mouse`\n- `open_git_diff()`, `close_diff_viewer()`\n- All three render call sites; `\"diff\"` removed from `NATIVE_VIEWS`\n- Palette entry \"Open Diff Viewer\"\n- Stale `default_tui.lua` docs rewritten to describe `focus_plugin` + plugin panels\n\n`/diff` is kept deliberately — it now prints where the feature went rather than silently doing nothing.\n\nTwo tests failed and were *correct* to: `every_accepted_action_name_is_dispatchable` and `documented_actions_are_all_handled` both asserted `diff_next_hunk` resolves. I inverted them to assert the removed names now resolve to `None`, so a future accidental re-add fails.\n\nVerification: workspace 47 suites green, clippy clean with zero dead-code warnings.\n\n## What you need to do\n\nThe running TUI still has the old binary in memory. Rebuild and trigger the plugin reload:\n\n```powershell\ncargo build -p kn9t-tui\n```\n\nThen in the TUI: `F10` and `/diff` should no longer open the Rust viewer. `Ctrl+G`