          "args_json": "{\"path\": \"./DIFF_REWORK_SUMMARY.md\", \"content\": \"# Diff Panel Rework: Executive Summary\\n\\n## Objective\\n**Move the Rust diff panel (1000+ lines) to a fully Lua-configurable plugin + system.**\\n\\nThis means:\\n- ✓ Users can fully customize diff UI/layout/keybinds\\n- ✓ Reduce Rust code by ~97%\\n- ✓ No loss of features\\n- ✓ All rendering, navigation, and keybinds become Lua-driven\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n### Where the diff panel lives today:\\n- **`crates/kn9t-tui/src/diff_viewer.rs`** (1000 lines)\\n  - Data structures: `DiffFile`, `DiffHunk`, `DiffLine`\\n  - UI state: `DiffViewer` struct with 10+ fields\\n  - Navigation: `next_hunk()`, `prev_file()`, `cursor_down()`, etc.\\n  - Rendering: `render()`, `render_split_mut()`, `render_unified_mut()`, `render_file_tree()`\\n  - Comments: `add_comment()`, `format_comments()`\\n  - Mouse: `handle_click()`, `handle_scroll()`\\n\\n- **`crates/kn9t-tui/src/app.rs`** (200 lines of diff logic)\\n  - Stores: `pub diff_viewer: Option<DiffViewer>`\\n  - Opens: `open_git_diff()` (parses git diff, creates DiffViewer)\\n  - Closes: `close_diff_viewer()` (extracts comments, appends to input)\\n  - Actions: All diff actions hardwired in `execute_action()` match statement\\n\\n- **`crates/kn9t-tui/src/ui/render.rs`** (400 lines of diff rendering)\\n  - `render_chat_overlays()` — fullscreen diff overlay\\n  - `render_native_view(\\\"diff\\\", ...)` — embedded diff (placed by Lua)\\n  - But the actual rendering is done by Rust: colors, syntax highlighting, layout\\n\\n- **`crates/kn9t-tui/src/keybind.rs`** (50 lines)\\n  - 11 hardcoded diff actions:\\n    - `DiffNextHunk`, `DiffPrevHunk`, `DiffNextFile`, `DiffPrevFile`\\n    - `DiffCursorUp`, `DiffCursorDown`, `DiffToggleSplit`, `DiffToggleFullscreen`\\n    - `DiffToggleTree`, `DiffComment`, `DiffClose`\\n  - Hardcoded key bindings (can be overridden in Lua, but defaults are rigid)\\n\\n### Key Input Handling:\\n```\\nhandle_key() → check diff_viewer.is_some() → handle_overlay_key() → hardcoded keycodes\\n```\\n\\n**Problem:** Users **cannot** customize:\\n- How the diff is laid out\\n- What colors are used\\n- What keys do what\\n- What extra actions are possible\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Proposed Solution\\n\\n### Phase 1: Plugin (NEW)\\nCreate **`crates/kn9t-plugin-diff`** (Rust, ~300 lines)\\n\\nExports `DiffPanel` struct:\\n- **Data:** `files: Vec<DiffFile>`, `current_file: usize`, `cursor_line: usize`, `scroll: usize`\\n- **Setters:** `set_current_file()`, `set_cursor_line()`, `set_scroll()`, `set_split_mode()`, `set_commenting()`\\n- **Getters:** `get_files()`, `get_current_file()`, `get_file_status()`, `get_comments_for_file()`\\n- **Methods:** `add_comment()`, `cancel_comment()`, `format_all_comments()`\\n\\n**Parsing:**\\n```rust\\npub fn parse_git_diff(diff_text: &str) -> DiffPanel { ... }\\n```\\n\\n**No rendering, no keybinding, no UI logic** — just data + state.\\n\\n### Phase 2: Lua (NEW)\\nCreate **`~/.kn9t/plugins/diff.lua`** (Lua, ~500 lines)\\n\\nHandles:\\n1. **Keybindings** — Users can bind any key to any action:\\n   ```lua\\n   kn9t.map('diff:next_file', function() ... end)\\n   kn9t.map('diff:custom_action', function() ... end)  -- NEW!\\n   ```\\n\\n2. **Rendering** — Full control over layout, colors, fonts:\\n   ```lua\\n   function diff.render_ui()\\n       return {\\n           type = 'vbox',\\n           children = {\\n               render_file_tree(),    -- Sidebar on left\\n               render_content(),      -- Main diff in middle\\n               render_footer(),       -- Stats at bottom\\n           }\\n       }\\n   end\\n   ```\\n\\n3. **Navigation logic** — Lua can do smarter things:\\n   ```lua\\n   kn9t.map('diff:next_hunk', function()\\n       -- Find next hunk header in virtual line list\\n       -- Auto-scroll to keep it visible\\n       -- Play a sound? Log an event? All possible in Lua!\\n   end)\\n   ```\\n\\n4. **Comments** — Lua input + plugin state:\\n   ```lua\\n   kn9t.map('diff:add_comment', function()\\n       panel:set_commenting(true, line_num)\\n       -- Render comment input box next frame\\n   end)\\n   ```\\n\\n### Phase 3: Rust Changes (MINIMAL)\\n**`crates/kn9t-tui/src/app.rs`:**\\n```rust\\n// Before:\\npub diff_viewer: Option<DiffViewer>\\n\\n// After:\\npub diff_panel: Option<Arc<Mutex<DiffPanel>>>  // from plugin\\n\\nfn open_git_diff(&mut self) {\\n    let text = std::process::Command::new(\\\"git\\\")\\n        .args(&[\\\"diff\\\", \\\"HEAD\\\"])\\n        .output()\\n        .map(|o| String::from_utf8(o.stdout).unwrap_or_default())\\n        .unwrap_or_default();\\n    \\n    // Call plugin\\n    self.diff_panel = Some(Arc::new(Mutex::new(\\n        kn9t_plugin_diff::parse_git_diff(&text)\\n    )));\\n}\\n\\nfn close_diff_viewer(&mut self) {\\n    let Some(panel) = self.diff_panel.take() else { return };\\n    let comments = panel.lock().unwrap().format_all_comments();\\n    self.input.push_str(&comments);\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**`crates/kn9t-tui/src/keybind.rs`:**\\n```rust\\n// Before: 11 diff actions\\nenum Action { DiffNextHunk, DiffPrevHunk, DiffNextFile, ... }\\n\\n// After: 1 diff action\\nenum Action { OpenDiff, ... }\\n\\n// All other diff keybinds are now in diff.lua\\n```\\n\\n**`crates/kn9t-tui/src/ui/render.rs`:**\\n- Remove: `render_split_mut()`, `render_unified_mut()`, `render_file_tree()`, all diff-specific rendering\\n- Keep: `render_ui()` (Lua controls it entirely)\\n\\n**`crates/kn9t-tui/src/diff_viewer.rs`:**\\n- Delete entirely (move data structures to plugin, delete rendering)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Features Preserved ✓\\n\\n| Feature | Current | New | Notes |\\n|---------|---------|-----|-------|\\n| Parse git diff | Rust | Plugin (Rust) | Same parser, now in plugin |\\n| File list | DiffViewer | DiffPanel | Same data structures |\\n| Hunk navigation | Rust nav methods | Lua logic | Lua reads file/hunk data |\\n| Line cursor | DiffViewer state | DiffPanel state | Same state, now mutable vi