          "text": "136 lines I didn't write — that's your in-flight work, like theme.rs. Leaving it alone.\n\nThe rework is complete and green. Summary:\n\n## What changed\n\n**New host primitives** (`crates/kn9t-tui/src/lua/plugin_ui.rs`)\n\nPlugin views went from render-only to genuinely interactive:\n- `kn9t.on_click(id, fn)` — clicks on widgets carrying that `id`\n- `kn9t.on_key(key, fn)` — keys while the view holds focus\n- `kn9t.insert_input(text)` — the one host mutation a view may request, queued as a `PluginEffect` (Lua callbacks have no `&mut App`, same as `kn9t.action`)\n\nHandlers are keyed `(plugin, id)`, so two plugins can reuse the same id or key without collision, and none can see or unbind another's. Keys only reach a **focused** view and `Esc` always blurs — so a plugin can't swallow `Ctrl+C` or trap focus. Returning `false` falls through to the host, matching `kn9t.map`'s existing contract. The sandbox is unchanged: still no `io`, no `os.execute`, no host globals.\n\nI also fixed a latent gap: `render_plugin_views` never collected clickable areas from plugin subtrees, so `id=` inside a plugin view was silently dead.\n\n**Plugin renamed** `kn9t-git-status` → `kn9t-git-integration`, and the `git_status` tool is **deleted**. Verified handshake: `hooks:[\"get_steering\"], tools:[]`. Bootstrap now rides `get_steering` (fires every turn with `session_id` + `cwd`) via the new `PluginHook::call_with_ctx`, which default-forwards to `call` so existing hooks are unaffected.\n\n**Diff view** lives in the plugin now: `diff.rs` parses (Rust runs `git` — it's a native process, unlike sandboxed Lua), `ui.lua` owns all rendering and input. File tree, split/unified, cursor, hunk nav, comments, click-to-select — all present.\n\n## Two bugs found and fixed\n\n1. **Comment line numbers.** The old viewer used `hunk.new_start + index`, which counts removed lines, so every comment after a deletion attached to the wrong line. Now tracked per-line during parse, with a regr