          "text": "Found the actual bug — and it's mine. The TUI log proves my Lua *did* load earlier (`plugin_ui kn9t-git-integration: ignoring unparseable key...`), so registration worked once. Then the TUI crashed and restarted.\n\n`poller.rs` sets `registered = true` after the first successful send and never re-sends. A TUI restart clears the host-side registry, but the plugin doesn't know — so `ui_set_state` keeps arriving with no source. Hence \"awaiting ui_register_lua\", permanently.",
