          "text": "All green, clippy clean. Here's what was actually wrong — four separate bugs, and you were right on every complaint.\n\n## Your three complaints, root-caused\n\n**1. \"Ctrl+G does nothing, just types g\"** — I invented that binding. It only exists in the *shipped* `default_tui.lua`, which your config overrides. Your layout uses **F10**. My advice was wrong, and the message telling you to press Ctrl+G was doubly wrong. Deleted the message and the `/diff` command entirely.\n\n**2. \"Palette view diff opens full black\"** — Your `90_render.lua` placed `{type=\"native\", view=\"diff\"}`, which I deleted. An unknown view renders as `Widget::Empty` — a black hole with no error. Fixed: the main pane now renders `{type=\"plugin\", plugin=\"kn9t-git-integration\"}`, with an explicit message if the plugin isn't registered.\n\n**3. \"Sidebar still shows kn9t-git-status waiting for first git_status call\"** — Your `30_sidebar_left.lua` hardcoded `GIT_PLUGIN_NAME = \"kn9t-git-status\"`. Renamed, and rewrote the placeholder, which described the tool-call bootstrap that no longer exists.\n\nYour `60_commands.lua` also still called `open_diff`/`diff_close`. The TUI log confirmed it: `Lua: unknown action 'open_diff'`. Now uses `focus_plugin`.\n\n## The \"awaiting ui_register_lua\" bug — mine\n\nThis was a genuine design error in `poller.rs`. I had it send the Lua source **once**, guarded by an `AtomicBool`, reasoning that re-sending was wasted work. But the **TUI** owns that registry and is a separate process. When it restarted (after the crash), its `plugin_ui` map was empty while the poller still believed it had registered — so every `ui_set_state` landed on a plugin with no `render()`, permanently.\n\nFixed by re-sending every poll. ~12 KB over a local pipe every 3s, and the host's `register()` replaces rather than accumulates. Idempotent re-send is the only thing that self-heals, since the protocol has no \"client reattached\" signal.\n\n## A fourth bug the log exposed\n\n`plugin_ui kn9t-git-integration: ignoring unparseable key 'Backspace'` — `parse_key` had no `Backspace`/`Delete` arm even though `key_event_to_string` emits exactly those names, and its `trim()` erased a literal `\" \"`. So backspace and space in the comment editor were silently dead. Both fixed, with a round-trip test that immediately caught me over-reaching on `Insert` (never emitted, so I scoped the test to reality rather than adding an unverifiable arm).\n\n## To try it\n\n```powershell\ncargo build -p kn9t-tui\n```\n\nRestart the TUI. The plugin binary also needs reinstalling — but `install-plugins --force` can't overwrite a running exe, so that needs the plugin process stopped first. Want me to handle that?\n\nThen: **F10** toggles the diff panel and focuses it; inside it `j`/`k`, `]`/`[`, `n`/`p`, `u`, `b`, `c`→type→`Enter`, `Ctrl+S`; **Esc** releases.\n\nNothing committed.",
